Changelog:
==========

**develop**
- add reusable contextual help popovers for Systems and Target filters
- build Systems and Target Preview from the same read-only Proxmox inventory
- unify active inventory projection for Systems and Target filters preview
- show immediate loading, success, and error feedback during web login
- add a read-only Target filters preview based on the current inventory and tag resolver
- regroup web UI configuration by host, guest type, filters, safety, and notifications
- hide internal host identifiers in user-facing details and job targets
- migrate compatible legacy SSH target files into targets.conf without deleting user configuration
- document the central External SSH setup, read-only checks, and restricted update helper
- bound remote cluster-check setup transfers so offline nodes cannot stall full checks
- preserve a non-zero final exit status after continuing past target failures
- show explicit per-node results in update summaries while keeping check summaries compact
- IMPORTANT: reboot the node after updating to this version before using the new session-independent update jobs
- detect pending Proxmox kernel reboots from selected bootable kernels
- avoid false interrupted states while transient systemd jobs are starting
- migrate and enable the web service during updater self-updates
- resolve Proxmox guest IDs cluster-wide for check/update commands
- preserve legacy update <ID> workflow across cluster nodes
- show Proxmox guest names in the Web UI
- expose cluster-remote update jobs through the calling node's CLI and Web UI
- refine the official Web UI header branding and node guest accordion layout
- use the official Ultimate Updater gear/update artwork in the web UI
- add web UI configuration for supported updater settings
- add web UI management for external SSH targets
- add Ultimate Updater branding and favicon
- run the web UI automatically as a systemd service
- organize the web UI by Proxmox node and external target
- add web UI check/update actions with persistent job status #314
- support Rocky/RHEL-family systems with dnf #313
- support Windows Update through QGA and PowerShell #312
- extend update-check notifications across all system targets #311
- support external apt-based systems over SSH #310
- run CLI updates through session-independent transient systemd jobs #316
- add a unified target/status CLI frontend #309
- separate shared target transport wrappers from existing updater paths #308
- add schema-versioned machine-readable check status output #306
- define optional target inventory and validate target-specific reachability data #305
- use a matching tag-filter helper for remote cluster checks #304
- synchronize USED_BRANCH with explicit branch updates #303
- simplify branch/version handling and cache remote versions for the welcome screen
- remove obsolete beta runtime handling and avoid network calls during SSH/MOTD login
- use exact guest ID matching and restore released #229 behavior #302
- fail LXC/SSH boot readiness after timeout #300
- compare version components numerically #301
- avoid empty VM startup delay in VM check path #299
- merge new config defaults without overwriting user values #298
- fix QEMU guest-exec exit-code and output handling #297
- fix duplicate command execution in error handlers #293
- add configurable backup storage in update.conf #269
- wait for QEMU Guest Agent readiness after starting stopped VMs #296
- harden Community-Scripts updates with timeout and error reporting #294
- add per-guest script-only update mode #243

